Geoid grids in this folder: egm2008_2.5min.nc and egm96_7.5min.nc
=====================================================================

These files are NOT covered by the BSD-3-Clause license of insardev_toolkit. They hold data of the US National
Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA), converted without adding any creative content, and are distributed under the
same terms as their sources: public domain.

EGM2008 (egm2008_2.5min.nc)
---------------------------
Source: PROJ-data grid us_nga_egm08_25.tif, https://cdn.proj.org/us_nga_egm08_25.tif
PROJ-data states for it (https://github.com/OSGeo/PROJ-data, files us_nga/us_nga_README.txt and
copyright_and_licenses.csv):

    *Source*: [NGA](http://earth-info.nga.mil/GandG/wgs84/gravitymod/egm2008/egm08_wgs84.html)
    *License*: Public Domain

    filename,copyright,license
    us_nga_egm08_25.tif,Disclaimed,Public domain

EGM96 (egm96_7.5min.nc)
-----------------------
Source: NGA EGM96 spherical harmonic coefficients EGM96 and CORRCOEF and NGA's program F477.F, as published on
http://earth-info.nga.mil/GandG/wgs84/gravitymod/egm96/egm96.html (archived copy:
https://web.archive.org/web/20061103210455/http://earth-info.nga.mil/GandG/wgs84/gravitymod/egm96/egm96.html).
PROJ-data distributes NGA's EGM96 15' grid from the same page with "License: Public Domain" (us_nga_egm96_15.tif).

NGA public-information notice
-----------------------------
https://www.nga.mil/resources/privacy.html (archived copy:
https://web.archive.org/web/20220421113353/https://www.nga.mil/resources/privacy.html):

    "Information presented on this Website is considered public information and may be distributed or copied
    unless otherwise specified. Use of appropriate byline/photo/image credits is requested."

Credit: EGM2008 and EGM96 geoid models, US National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA); EGM96 jointly with NASA
Goddard Space Flight Center.

